WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.540
The 2010s produced anime like never before.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:08.759
Tales of love, magic, and betrayal flooded
the airwaves on all manner of devices, reaching

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.980
all manner of people.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.440
Here's to the best anime of the decade, and
to another ten years of ice skating, ping

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.040
pong, and magical girl deconstruction.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.340
Madoka Magica might be a franchise that spans
mobile games, multiple movies, and a wealth

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:26.660
of spin-off manga, but its earlier success
came from its economy of story.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:32.020
At only 12 episodes, the original series is
a succinct marvel; no plot is extraneous,

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.000
all foreshadowing pays off, and the pacing
is steady and certain.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.710
There are no skippable episodes of Madoka,
no moments that don't matter.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:44.200
It is a journey that has to be taken step
by step, into a forest that grows steadily

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:44.880
darker.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.559
Much has been made of this darkness.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.160
And it's true that Madoka gained early fame
as a deconstruction of magical girl stories,

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.199
and still stands out against a field of imitators.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:59.640
But it's here too that Madoka's brevity shines,
and where it can be seen with the greatest clarity.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:05.120
Madoka grows from a naive young girl into
a terrified pawn, but only for a couple of episodes.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.200
It's then, in the depths of despair, that
she realizes her power, seizes it, and changes

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.250
the world forever.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.780
The momentum this creates is felt on the most
visceral level, catapulting the viewer from

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.310
horror into awe within one episode.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:23.270
For all the talk of deconstruction surrounding
the series, at its core, Madoka is that greatest

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:28.620
of magical girl stories: it looks cruelty
in the eye, spins its magic wand, and tells

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.620
it to take a hike.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.800
For all its splendid animation, One Punch
Man's most famous moment is probably its simplest:

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.540
This set of armor used to seal in my immeasurable, irresistible power...

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.920
...has been broken.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.220
Ok.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.780
We love watching Saitama him absorb punches
from undersea monsters.

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:52.500
We love watching him take out hyper-advanced
robots.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.540
But we love his deadpan reactions to the bizarre
world around him even more.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.340
That's because it's emblematic of what makes
One Punch Man so special: it absolutely loves

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.119
making fun of superheroes.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:09.120
Now, One Punch Man loves superheroes, and
specifically, being a superhero series.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.120
But its love is flexible, as devoted to jaw-dropping
moments of action as it is to the goofiness

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.920
of animal-themed bad guys.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.780
You have your dudes like Genos, who genuinely
looks awesome most of the time, but you also

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.000
have villains like Crablante, walking around
like a lobster in tighty-whities.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.940
There is no contradiction between the two
in the world of One Punch Man, they're all

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.650
part of the same bright, bizarre tapestry.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.570
Superpowers, robots, ninjas, mad scientists
are all there to be loved, feared, and made

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:41.390
fun of, and in so doing, One Punch Man has
more fun with them all than most other series

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.900
of its ilk combined.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.880
Saitama is the guy of the meme, the guy of
the wickedly cool fight compilations, and

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.540
the guy who loves a weekly sale at the grocery
store.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.600
He, and his anime, contain multitudes, and
that's why we love them.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:59.280
Describing Ping Pong: The Animation is a fool's
errand, but here's what we can tell you for

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.980
sure: Ping Pong is about high school boys
playing ping pong.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:07.430
If you're at all interested, and maybe even
if you're not, it's worth watching the 11

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:11.920
episodes that make up this bizarre, brilliant,
bewildering gem of an anime.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.260
Adapted from the manga by Taiyo Matsumoto,
Ping Pong retains its distinctively weird,

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.310
ungainly look, but that's the point: weird,
wondrous experimentation.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:26.010
It takes a delirious sort of delight in alienating
its viewer, using everything from jarring

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:30.940
amounts of negative space to superimposed
comic panels to keep its audience adrift in

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.470
a sea of the unexpected.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:37.330
Ping Pong is about the towering possibilities
of animation, the ferocious thrill of sport,

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:41.120
and the power of art to confuse viewers as
readily as it clarifies.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.640
It is also about ping pong.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.580
Somehow, it makes sense, and in so doing,
it triumphs.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.080
Nerds had a good time in the 2010s.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:54.200
Video games rocketed to new heights of sophistication,
superheroes dominated the box office, and

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.890
everything from She-Ra to Blade Runner got
a reboot.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:02.600
Still, many nerds still languish on the margins
as weirdos, geeks, and outcasts.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.780
The women of Princess Jellyfish, clustered
together in an all-woman boarding house for

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.860
unmarried "nuns," as they call themselves,
live very much within this societal shadow.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:17.260
They are awkward, obsessed with trains, utterly
terrified of social situations, and more interested

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:20.940
in talking about Legend of the Three Kingdoms
lore than dating.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.720
When a gorgeous new neighbor upsets their
lives, quickly followed by the threat of neighborhood

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.860
developers seizing their home, they find they
have to change, but they have no idea how.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:35.640
What makes Princess Jellyfish so special isn't
how keenly it observes the lives of its shut-in

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.700
heroines, but how deeply it empathizes with
them.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:43.420
Sure, the series indulges in a few makeover
sequences, but the makeup comes off at the

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.620
end of the day, and no one has to give up
their doll collection.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:51.150
These characters aren't forced into new situations
because they deserve anxiety, but to show

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:55.850
them that they can endure it, and that they
were stronger than they realized all along.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:05:00.120
They are who they are, and that's the source
of the show's humor, but it's also the heart

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.800
of the series, only grown larger by its end.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:08.340
Little Witch Academia captures the magic of
being a child on the edge of adulthood, in

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.540
addition to quite a bit of literal magic,
with a rare and thrilling joy.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:17.191
The story of an academy of girls learning
the art and science of witchcraft, Little

00:05:17.191 --> 00:05:22.240
Witch Academia never loses sight of that breathless
moment when a kid realizes the world is far

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.310
stranger and more vast than they'd ever before
realized, and that their role within it might

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.860
take them to places they've never even imagined.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.360
I can be!

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.700
I will be an amazing witch through my own hard work.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.720
This is especially remarkable when one remembers
just how many elements the anime encompasses.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:46.000
In just two seasons, Little Witch Academia
manages to squeeze in stories about fire-breathing

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.920
dragons, competing academies, fairy laborers
on strike, the ancient lineage of magic, and

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:54.000
literal nuclear warfare.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.080
Taken in full, this isn't just a collection
of delightful tales but a verdant garden of

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.430
story, far greater than the sum of its parts.

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:07.230
The world of Akko, Diana, and all their friends
and teachers feels real because it is comprised

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:12.810
of so many different parts, appropriately,
as Luna Nova is, after all, a school of magic

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.400
that brings in international students from
many different walks of life.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.970
The anime that results is an endlessly entertaining
tale of youth's possibility, which might just

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.800
be the greatest magic of all.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:30.360
Anime in 2010 was dominated with an endless
parade of little sisters, schoolgirls, pre-teen

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.060
vampire queens, and otherwise idealized child-women.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:38.520
That's the landscape that Panty and Stocking
were lobbed onto like a grenade.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:43.050
Here were two characters who had literally
been expelled from heaven for being unladylike.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:47.580
Sure, they aim to get back in, but not by
changing their ways: They end the series as

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.270
lascivious and dessert-loving as they began
it.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:54.840
They're just planning to smash enough bad
guys down on Earth that the man upstairs decides

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:55.890
to look the other way.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:01.400
Inspired by everything from Cartoon Network's
greatest '90s hits to tokusatsu tv shows,

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.100
Panty and Stocking wears its shape-shifting
heart on its sleeve.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:09.660
Some episodes combine the lowest lowbrow gags
with genuine romance.

00:07:09.669 --> 00:07:13.260
Demons are thwarted by a total commitment
to lustful abandon.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:18.169
An episode-length parody of the Transformers
franchise manages to tell an actual story

00:07:18.169 --> 00:07:19.500
about sibling rivalry.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:24.240
It's a glorious, explosive mess of a series
unlike anything else of its era.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.240
Panty and Stocking are creatures of appetite
and altruism in equal measure, and their anime

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.490
adores them for it.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:35.889
They are, like the series itself, bizarre,
crude, loud, and heartfelt, and the decade

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:37.300
is better off for containing them.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.200
Kids on the Slope

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:43.480
Kids on the Slope was always going to be notable,
even if it had ended up an utter failure.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:49.330
It brought Shinichiro Watanabe, legendary
anime director, and Yoko Kanno, equally legendary

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:53.740
composer, back together for the first time
since the iconic Cowboy Bebop.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.240
It could have used its pedigree to slack off.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.100
It could have settled for mediocrity.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.240
People still would have watched Kids on the
Slope, probably even praised it.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.680
It did not really have to try.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:04.500
But it did.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:09.880
Kids on Slope doesn't just succeed, it dazzles,
and in an entirely different way than Watanabe

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.100
and Kanno's previous collaboration.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:17.940
Centered around a group of teenagers living
in 1966, the anime is a soulful slice of adolescent

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:22.540
discovery, postwar reconstruction, and the
transporting power of music.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:27.380
It's tempting to call the story slow, but
that isn't quite right, but Kids on the Slope

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:28.560
is unhurried.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:34.360
It's a true pleasure to lose one's self in
its mists of teenage longing and jazz standards,

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:39.120
but when taken as a whole, what emerges is
a story of uncommon emotional force.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.860
Like the music it loves, the series wanders
on its way to where it's going, losing itself

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.040
in spirals of emotion and art.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:51.550
But when it gets there, the viewer realizes
the journey was as important as the destination,

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.940
and all the more meaningful for its unique
rhythms.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.600
Will anything exemplify the 2010s more than
the superhero?

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:03.430
Movies, TV, toys, video games, and of course,
comic books, spent the decade in a passionate

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.589
embrace with that most 20th century of genres.

00:09:06.589 --> 00:09:12.760
Anime is no exception; My Hero Academia is
one of the 2010s' greatest success stories.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:16.930
In combining superheroes with high school,
it didn't just strike gold, but also made

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:19.800
the whole world wonder why this hadn't happened
before.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.660
Teenagers with powers, fighting evil and decorating
their dorms?

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:26.580
It's everything anime and comic nerds ever
needed.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:31.400
But My Hero Academia has proven over and over
again that its success goes far beyond the

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:32.820
chemistry of its premise.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:38.160
In making its hero Deku, a boy who is never
guaranteed any win, it's managed to capture

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.180
the sort of magic that defined American superhero
comics' Golden Age.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.760
Deku doesn't watch All Might videos over and
over again just because they're cool, he watches

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:50.520
them because he loves the moment the people
in crisis are told that everything will be

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:51.280
all right.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:57.000
He rejoices when he's granted fabulous abilities,
not because he can now heft a dump truck,

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:01.600
but because he can now become that person
who takes away fear, worry, and pain.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:06.500
I want to be the greatest hero, like you!

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:11.630
My Hero Academia is about superheroes in their
purest form: people with the power to keep

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:12.710
others safe.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:18.320
In centering that, it has become an anime
that will be loved far beyond this one cape-crazy decade.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:23.120
Figure skating is the sort of world that practically
begs for an anime.

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:24.600
Sparkly costumes!

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.880
Opportunities for dramatic animation!

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.260
Attractive people thrust into highly tense
situations!

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:35.860
Yuri on Ice had no shortage of story opportunities
to pick from, and it savored each and every one.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.420
Tears were shed, lots and lots of tears, in
fact.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:42.940
Emotions were expressed through axels and
Salchows.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:46.460
International relations were threatened by
drunken faux-pas.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.740
It was, from beginning to end, an absolute
delight.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.820
But Yuri on Ice never settled for mere spectacle.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:58.460
Its moments of indulgence, extravagant routines,
scantily-clad athletes, flamboyant costumes,

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:01.920
were all in service to the tender love story
at its core.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.740
Yuri and Victor's relationship blooms in the
cracks between punishing practice and high-stakes

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:12.730
competition, threatened at all times by failure,
skill gaps, and the inexorable march of age.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:17.420
But it cannot be quashed, and indeed, by the
end of the series, it has overtaken the obstacles

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:20.040
in its way like they weren't even there to
begin with.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:24.580
This is an anime about giving your life over
to something and finding it never loses the

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.360
capacity to surprise you.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.710
Sometimes you end up with a case full of awards.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.260
Sometimes you end up in love.

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:34.940
Yuri on Ice is about both of these things,
and all the beauty, magic, and adventure one

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:35.980
finds in between.

